  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed as a suru verb ({破壊|はかい}する = to destroy) or as a noun modifier ({破壊|はかい}{力|りょく} = destructive power). Very commonly appears in the passive ({破壊|はかい}される = to be destroyed). The compound {環境|かんきょう}{破壊|はかい} (environmental destruction) is an extremely frequent set phrase.\n\nWRITING:\n{破|は} means \"to break\" and {壊|かい} means \"to destroy.\" Both characters carry the meaning of destruction, making this a reinforcing compound.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {環境|かんきょう}{破壊|はかい}: environmental destruction\n- {破壊|はかい}{力|りょく}: destructive power\n- {破壊|はかい}{的|てき}: destructive\n- {大量|たいりょう}{破壊|はかい}{兵器|へいき}: weapons of mass destruction\n- {自己|じこ}{破壊|はかい}: self-destruction",
